  "checkpoint": "MSC-122 profile status propagation and personal API/MCP boundaries",
  "date": "2026-10-11",
  "status": "Qualified component batch on KVM and serial monolith. Remaining chat/profile dependencies and community-free composition are open; template work remains paused.",
  "changes": [
    "ProfileStatusWork consumes account-owned ProfileStatusObserver. Native and remote UserAffinityChanges forward once to the existing affinity status queue; work marker, support-message order, scoped calls and retry behavior are unchanged.",
    "McpAuthorizationService delegates only workspace-specific checks and name lookup to GroupMcpWorkspaceAccess. Personal authorization can start without that provider. The full application keeps its account reads, workspace selection, null-name semantics, redirect/PKCE checks and owner failures.",
    "IntegrationCapabilitiesService retains authentication and role checks. GroupIntegrationCapabilities owns the unchanged product operation list and group scope checks; the generic implementation advertises the existing chat/notification reads without a product provider.",
    "Four existing chat/notification GET routes moved to IntegrationCommunicationReadController. URL mappings, actor selection, response DTOs, pagination bounds and markViewed=false are unchanged; both controllers share the original bounds/not-found helpers.",
    "The existing runtime profile-selection harness now also reads MCP client settings and OAuth metadata. It does not call the general API settings route because that existing GET may create an affiliate link."
  ],
